<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GSSO_000485> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A broad term that includes all diseases, lesions, disorders, or nonpathologic condition that normally receives medical treatment, such as pregnancy or childbirth." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GSSO_000485> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Any kind of illness or circumstance which requires medical monitoring." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GSSO_000485> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GSSO_000485> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "medical condition" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GSSO_000485> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GSSO_000484> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GSSO_000486> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Any condition that impairs the normal functioning of the body. For this reason, diseases are associated with dysfunctioning of the body's normal homeostatic processes." .
